in is for their entire stack (20,000), meaning I would have to call 19,800 more to match (since I already put in 200). This is a huge commitment with a weak hand. Given that this is the 19th hand out of 20, and I currently have a chip lead (19750 vs opponent's stack, likely similar or less due to all-in), folding preserves my lead and avoids risking almost all my chips on a marginal hand. The only viable actions are all-in or fold, and all-in here would be extremely risky without a strong hand.\n\nReason: Calling all-in with 10-9 offsuit is not justified; the opponent could have a much stronger range. Folding allows me to maintain my chip advantage going into the final hand, maximizing my chance to win the overall game by avoiding a massive unnecessary risk. Since the cumulative win/loss is separate, my current chip stack is what matters for winning this hand and the game.\n\nAnswer: -1"}
